From b7f46f04d1798a8dda31d5770833127ea0b42c72 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christian Hewitt <christianshewitt@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 12:40:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 139/145] media: meson: vdec: sort the format tables by pixel
 format

The tables grew in the order support was added, which by now is no
order at all: VP9 first on some platforms and last on none, H.264
before HEVC on some and after it on others, and the codecs added most
recently simply appended.  Sort every table by pixel format so a
platform's coverage can be read off, and so the difference between two
platforms is the entries they do not share.

The entries themselves are untouched, but this is not quite a no-op:
vdec_open() takes formats[0] as the session's default OUTPUT format and
its first capture format, so the default becomes H.263 rather than
whatever each platform happened to list first.  Every client sets the
format it wants before streaming, and the capture format is NV12M
either way, so nothing in practice reads the default - but ENUM_FMT
order changes with it, and a client that queries G_FMT before setting
one sees something different.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Christian Hewitt <christianshewitt@gmail.com>
